    "status": "open",
    "gate": "LGSWF-073",
    "requires": [
      "WorkPacket@1 is the single canonical daemon packet; existing implementation-daemon envelopes extend in place and never introduce a parallel packet format",
      "WorkPacket@1 binds every required goal, plan, repository, semantic, symbol, capsule, source, contract, proof, context, scope, resource, provider, model, validation, completion, lease, fence, attempt, idempotency, checkpoint, cancellation, and output field under one content-addressed schema",
      "CheckpointProtocol@1 exposes the closed main lifecycle offered through accepted and the full side-path taxonomy rejected/blocked/cancelled/timed_out/failed/partial_effect/compensation_required/superseded/quarantined",
      "bounded attempt checkpoints bind attempt, plan revision, semantic root, worktree tree, changed files/symbols, stage, resources, model calls, tests, proofs, outstanding obligations, effects, resume needs, and checkpoint_cid without implying completion",
      "resume requires a verified authority binding over plan, semantic root, lease, fence, and scope digests; foreign or unbound checkpoints fail closed",
      "typed stale stops fire immediately on plan_changed, supersession, semantic_root_changed, lease_changed, fence_changed, scope_changed, cancellation, or prior_acceptance and never allow finish after authority loss",
      "scope enforcement binds read_scope, write_scope, allowed_edit_paths, and effects into content-addressed scope digests; scope drift is a typed stale stop",
      "fabric mode makes active PlanRevisionStore, shared coordination, resource admission, packet identity, checkpoint recovery, stale fencing, and sealed launcher protections non-optional on ImplementationDaemon and MultiSupervisorRunner",
      "acceptance requires supervisor_verified then accepted; worker completion or task status alone never authorizes acceptance",
      "binary floats are excluded from content-addressed packet, checkpoint, authority-binding, and typed-stale-stop identities",
      "model proposals remain non-authoritative and never admit work"
    ],
    "prior_status": "Epic G open for dependency-ready work; Epic H unblocks adaptive revision and refill"
